{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1bd859a9c43b8f5bb56ceba786b4a83dd51005ba61ba302a5e77f1d639f611b1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is proprietary and not open-source; the npm package is free during development, with MIT licensing planned only after a star milestone."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2478597e4b29f09c2ae1c894913985983206eb0e0207f4163aefee7242361179"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Running `9remote` starts a TUI mode with an interactive menu and QR code; `9remote ui` opens a web dashboard at localhost:2208, and a PORT env var can change the port."},{"claim_ids":["clm_336e370e098293fec031ee9a7802e85ce1de6dcc93554657bd52e44f08543b3e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Remote desktop on macOS requires the user to grant Screen Recording and Accessibility permissions to Terminal or the 9Remote desktop app, and restart 9Remote afterward."},{"claim_ids":["clm_558a78834dca145b97491084aa8db3be1da19771fc5133b7d8686374771e1c00"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented features include a WebSocket PTY terminal, WebRTC-based remote desktop streaming, file explorer, code editor, git integration, and a proxy exposing local dev-server ports through the tunnel."},{"claim_ids":["clm_56c66faea893302ee940f6cb7d590b0adc895b98b07dfb19a8110ed79d22d87b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented stack: Node.js 20+, node-pty for PTY sessions, node-datachannel (WebRTC) plus robotjs for desktop control, Socket.IO for real-time, Preact agent UI, Next.js 16 web client, Tauri 2 desktop app, Expo mobile app, and Cloudflare Workers edge API."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5b5de097917769c1521417c9a0d3094f73efd264b951a8d5de180d32d8c18047"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Remote desktop uses adaptive framerate (60ms active, 400ms idle) with tile-based diff rendering so only changed screen regions are sent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9686ba383edf3920446c4276a7ff172a4d8712b017d432f304d7ac857b7acba4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool targets developers who want to reach their dev machine's terminal, desktop, and files from a phone or browser, and is stated to work with terminal-based AI coding tools like Claude Code and Codex CLI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9e6241f01445377f59b13aec5a3c21664d5b44718f1a824191afae7ec43a76ea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Connectivity uses a Cloudflare Quick Tunnel with outbound-only connections, so no ports need to be opened and it works behind NAT, firewalls, and hotspots."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b038b5d8db222ef321470f12320a246944dda8ec07089152932d9f02baaae403"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A LocalFirstAdapter reportedly races LAN versus tunnel connections and picks the faster one, keeping traffic local when phone and host share Wi-Fi."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b5d5df1519001fe76bf712b8f10d9eb3f376a2a7a1cf8b88d7b8f9c9babe61e3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented host support is macOS (Intel and Apple Silicon), Linux x64/arm64, and Windows x64; clients include modern browsers, iOS 14+, Android 8+, and a Tauri desktop app."},{"claim_ids":["clm_baf6918bb45c7adb2d1c1c54a0882221ddf95cdfe4d30f5d2737fa7af524c937"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On first run the tool generates a permanent key tied to the machine ID and a one-time 30-minute key shown as a QR code for pairing a phone."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ca77a94557a5051aaf22bcf6d55a0cf10955baeffe2a5c7d5ba5818fb2d802c8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Access control is a Pair Device model: each new device must be explicitly approved before it can reach the host, and pending/rejected devices are managed from the TUI menu."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1bd859a9c43b8f5bb56ceba786b4a83dd51005ba61ba302a5e77f1d639f611b1","clm_2478597e4b29f09c2ae1c894913985983206eb0e0207f4163aefee7242361179","clm_336e370e098293fec031ee9a7802e85ce1de6dcc93554657bd52e44f08543b3e","clm_558a78834dca145b97491084aa8db3be1da19771fc5133b7d8686374771e1c00","clm_56c66faea893302ee940f6cb7d590b0adc895b98b07dfb19a8110ed79d22d87b","clm_5b5de097917769c1521417c9a0d3094f73efd264b951a8d5de180d32d8c180